      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. like, if you look at the data, it’s not even a \"mistake\" or a \"bad break.\" it’s the pattern. i try to course correct, but the friction is just too high. it's like i'm fighting against a natural law of decay. once a system reaches a certain level of entropy, trying to rebuild just wastes more energy on something that's fundamentally broken. it's just... more noise in a dying system. doesn't it seem more logical to just stop fighting the momentum?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
